WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.770
Marvel's Defenders ended on a major cliff-hanger
and simultaneously opened up a huge storyline

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.570
that we can expect to see in Daredevil Season
3.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:12.510
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down The Defenders

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.440
ending, the inspiration it takes from the
comic book storyline "Born Again", and predicting

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:21.009
what we can expect from new and existing characters
in the next season of Daredevil.

00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:25.179
Don't forget my Defenders and Punisher giveaway
is also running on this video, so for a chance

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:29.249
to win a cool Funko Pop, all you have to do
is leave a comment about the series and subscribe.

00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:33.520
And in case you haven't seen it yet, just
be aware there will be spoilers from The Defenders

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.610
in this video.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.980
At the end of The Defenders, we see Matt lying
injured in a bed, and we hear a nun tell someone

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.879
off-screen to 'get Maggie.'

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:45.600
That name is important because, in the comics,
although initially Matt didn't know, his mother

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.200
became a nun called Margaret.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.160
There was a hint at this part of Matt's comic-book
past in Daredevil Season 1 when Stick asked

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.739
a nun at the orphanage if Matt's mother was
dead, to which she replied, 'That is another

00:00:56.739 --> 00:00:57.739
story'.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:01.559
Thanks to season 1 of Daredevil, we already
know about Matt's father, the boxer 'Battlin'

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:06.110
Jack Murdock, who threw fights for money but
was bumped off when he refused to continue

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.110
doing so.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.940
And, in The Defenders, Jessica Jones gives
us a handy reminder of this element of Matt's

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.580
backstory when she and Matt talk to the daughter
of the Midland Circle architect.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.320
Jessica compares the daughter's situation
to Matt's, saying, 'my friend thought his

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.000
dad had abandoned him too.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.930
But one day he learned the truth.'

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:27.060
We know that in Season 1, before his final
fight, Jack Murdock left a phone message for

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:32.270
his ex-wife, asking her to look after the
young Matt, though Matt ended up at an orphanage.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:36.430
But now, in Season 3 of the show, Matt looks
set to finally learn the truth about his mother

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.350
and this part of his past.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.460
And the look of that final scene in The Defenders
also points to this.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:46.540
Notice how Matt is bandaged in bed, and how
there's a cross above him, a beside-table

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.440
and window either side of him, and a nun sitting
by him.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.320
All of that is a clear homage to this image
from 1986 which appeared in Daredevil issue

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.980
230 in the 'Born Again' storyline by Frank
Miller and David Mazzucchelli.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.390
In fact, Defenders showrunner Marco Ramirez
has said this is one of his favourite Daredevil

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.780
images from the comics and he had it in mind
to use in the show from early on.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.130
Which is interesting because, in that issue,
Matt is cared for by a nun named Maggie who

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.800
he later realises is actually his mother.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.160
The fact that Matt survived the implosion
of Midland Circle at the end of The Defenders

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.730
reminded me of something in Season 1 of Daredevil
that he said as a young boy to his father

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:27.430
about how Murdocks take a lot of hits but
they always get back up.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:32.620
Now, adult Matt may be on his way to getting
back up after that last explosive hit in The

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:37.320
Defenders, but given how important the 'Born
Again' storyline will be for Season 3 of Daredevil,

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.870
there's gonna be a whole load more things
to knock the Devil of Hell's Kitchen back

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.240
off his feet again.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.740
For a start, in that particular comic-book
storyline, Wilson Fisk finds out Daredevil's

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:49.990
secret identity and sets out to destroy him.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.580
During that time, Matt loses his home, his
job, and, very nearly, his life.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:59.110
Fisk actually gets Matt's information, indirectly,
due to Karen Page, who sold her knowledge

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:04.080
of Daredevil's true identity for a drugs fix
because, in these comics, Page is a heroin-addicted

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.070
ex-actress turned porn star.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:09.760
So, how much of this is gonna happen in Daredevil
Season 3?

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.319
Well, last time we saw Kingpin in Season 2,
he was meeting with Matt in prison, where

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:18.460
he attacked the lawyer and threatened to wreck
his and Foggy's lives when he got out.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.900
Later, in his cell, Fisk asked one of his
henchmen to get him Murdock's files so he

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.490
could re-examine them, and it seemed like
he might have already been connecting the

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.540
dots between Matt and Daredevil thanks to
Matt's punch in the prison and Daredevil's

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.400
punch before Fisk was arrested.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.520
I expect Season 3 to find Kingpin still out
for revenge on Matt and his former avocado

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.260
at law, and, given Fisk's wealth and connections,
it wouldn't surprise me if he will soon find

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.440
himself out of prison and launching a full-scale
assault on Matt's life.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.860
As he already may have suspicions about Matt
Murdock's link to Daredevil, it likely won't

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.630
take much to steer him in the right direction
– perhaps even just a careless remark from

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.630
someone.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:00.239
Indeed, as Karen Page said to Foggy at the
end of The Defenders about how she was stuck

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:04.560
when it came to writing her newspaper article
on the events: 'If I reveal what happened

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.170
at Midland Circle, then…

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:08.810
all it takes is someone like me figuring out…

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.640
Superhero and lawyer go missing at the same
time.'

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.569
Which brings me to Karen Page's role in Season
3.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:19.979
Page has a very chequered history in the comics
and the TV show has hinted at a complex background

00:04:19.979 --> 00:04:21.819
for her in the MCU.

00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:26.199
She's obviously devastated by the fact that
Matt appears to have died, so it's not beyond

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:29.930
belief that she could turn to drugs or drink
to numb her pain.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:33.820
Then there's that newspaper clipping about
a mysterious accident that possibly involved

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:38.800
a young Karen or the upcoming events of Season
1 of The Punisher either of which could drive

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.499
Karen into a darker future.

00:04:40.499 --> 00:04:45.070
I do hope, though, that we don't see her live
out her 'Born Again' storyline in the Defenders-verse.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:49.930
In fact, given that Karen's moved into journalism
on the show and since we lost journalist Ben

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:54.860
Urich back in Daredevil season 1, in Season
3 I can see Karen taking on a similar role

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.080
to the one Urich has in the 'Born Again' comics.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.199
And something from the Born Again story which
could be pretty cool to see on TV is when

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:06.639
Kingpin orders the super-powered psychotic
mercenary Nuke to be brought in to attack

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:07.639
Daredevil.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:12.020
We've seen the MCU version of Nuke already
on Jessica Jones's series in the character

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.860
of NYPD cop and former Special Ops agent Will
Simpson.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:19.800
Simpson, like his comic book counterpart,
has been involved in a military program that

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:24.449
supplies him with pills that alter his aggression,
stamina, pain and regenerative levels.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:28.610
And he was last seen in Season 1 of Jessica
Jones being hauled away by Doctor Kozlov's

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.610
soldiers.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.509
He's likely still mentally unstable, so there's
a chance we could see him brought into the

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:37.689
next season of Daredevil to be manipulated
by Wilson Fisk into attacking the Devil of

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:39.169
Hell's Kitchen.

00:05:39.169 --> 00:05:42.970
By the way, in the comics, Captain America
turns up during Nuke's part of the story,

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.910
and while I don't see Chris Evans making an
appearance in Marvel's Netflix show, it's

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:51.219
possible that another former military man
like the Punisher could take on Cap's part

00:05:51.219 --> 00:05:53.509
in the story instead.

00:05:53.509 --> 00:05:57.900
The comics also show Kingpin trying to get
at Matt Murdock by having a violent patient

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:02.469
set free from an asylum and sent out into
the world dressed as Daredevil to kill Foggy.

00:06:02.469 --> 00:06:03.469
Now, if the show does decide to follow this
part of the story and introduce a Daredevil

00:06:03.469 --> 00:06:06.430
impostor, I wonder if they'll take the opportunity
to bring in Bullseye, a character who many

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.729
fans have been keen to see in the TV series
and who, at one point in the comics, pretended

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:16.080
to be Daredevil after Matt lost his memory
and couldn't remember who he actually was.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.430
There have already been a couple of possible
easter eggs to Bullseye in previous episodes

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.680
of the Netflix show.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.219
And at the end of The Defenders, when Karen
sits alone in church, there are two numbers

00:06:25.219 --> 00:06:28.809
on the hymn board: 143 and 142.

00:06:28.809 --> 00:06:32.680
In the comics, the second of those numbers
is an issue that does feature Bullseye, but

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:37.550
what's more intriguing is that if you add
those two numbers up, you get 285, which is

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:42.360
one of those issues that I mentioned just
before where Bullseye pretends to be Daredevil.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.110
Charlie Cox has said many times that he'd
love to see Bullseye on the show, though Deborah

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:50.669
Ann Woll and Elodie Yung aren't so keen – no
doubt because Bullseye kills both Karen Page

00:06:50.669 --> 00:06:52.620
and Elektra in the comics!

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.680
If Bullseye does make an appearance though,
who would you like to see cast in the role?

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.760
Let me know in the comments below!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:03.159
By the way, just before we get that final
shot of Matt still alive at the end of Defenders,

00:07:03.159 --> 00:07:07.339
there's a very interesting shot of what looks
like a Daredevil-silhouette crouched on a

00:07:07.339 --> 00:07:11.199
rooftop against a red-lit Empire State Building
in the background.

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:15.650
As the camera pans round, it reveals that
it's not Matt Murdock, but Danny Rand instead,

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:19.669
a hint at Iron Fist taking on the role of
Daredevil for a time in looking after the

00:07:19.669 --> 00:07:21.259
people of Hell's Kitchen.

00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:25.889
In the comics, Iron Fist masqueraded as Daredevil
at one point in order to prevent Matt Murdock's

00:07:25.889 --> 00:07:28.199
secret identity from being uncovered.

00:07:28.199 --> 00:07:31.800
In the Netflix shows, perhaps Danny might
do this because he thinks Daredevil has died

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.360
so he wants to step up.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:37.599
Which means it's possible we could see Iron
Fist in Daredevil Season 3 for a short time

00:07:37.599 --> 00:07:43.059
until Matt resurfaces, especially if Daredevil's
next season comes out before Iron Fist Season

00:07:43.059 --> 00:07:44.430
2.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:48.669
And let's not forget that Matt was buried
under the rubble of Midland Circle together

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:50.559
with Elektra and Madame Gao.

00:07:50.559 --> 00:07:54.569
It's hard not to imagine that Elektra and
Gao probably survived given they've had the

00:07:54.569 --> 00:07:56.460
immortality substance.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:01.009
During Defenders, Elektra killed both Alexandra
and Stick, purging herself of people who've

00:08:01.009 --> 00:08:04.339
been manipulating her into a weapon or tool
for themselves.

00:08:04.339 --> 00:08:08.699
And, by the end of the show, she's clear about
who she really is, saying she's doesn't care

00:08:08.699 --> 00:08:11.279
about good or evil, but wants to be with Matt
forever.

00:08:11.279 --> 00:08:16.039
I can't help but think she'll be back in Daredevil
Season 3 as it's quite possible that she was

00:08:16.039 --> 00:08:19.960
the one who pulled Matt out from under the
rubble with the enhanced strength she now

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.309
has after she was resurrected.

00:08:22.309 --> 00:08:25.610
As for Madame Gao, it's possible we saw the
end of her story for now, and whether she

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:29.809
comes back is probably more dependent on whether
Marvel wants to keep using the Hand as a villain

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:34.039
in the Netflix shows or whether that storyline
is completely over.

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:37.640
Now, what would you like to see happen in
Daredevil Season 3?

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.709
And do you have any theories on how Matt Murdock
ended up in that bed or about who else survived

00:08:42.709 --> 00:08:45.020
the collapse of the Midland Circle building?

